BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Domain-Aware Workflow Monitoring in Open OnDemand - Owen Schillaci
  [Texas A&M University]
DTSTART;TZID=US/Mountain:20260311T110000
DTEND;TZID=US/Mountain:20260311T112500
DTSTAMP:20261020T211455Z
UID:pretalx-good-2026-DSFY7V@pretalx.com
DESCRIPTION:Researchers rely on Open OnDemand (OOD) to design\, launch\, a
 nd manage scientific workflows on high performance computing (HPC) systems
 . In addition to job creation and submission\, this process also includes 
 monitoring job progress. OOD provides the job-listing app and session card
 s for monitoring running jobs. However\, these tools primarily provide sch
 eduler-level information\, forcing researchers to manually retrieve workfl
 ow and domain-specific information. Drona Workflow Engine bridges this gap
  by providing integrated\, domain-specific monitoring throughout the workf
 low lifecycle. In this presentation\, we will focus on job-monitoring capa
 bilities and explore various types of job monitoring integrated into the r
 epresentative\, commonly used scientific workflows.
LOCATION:Breakout Room
URL:https://pretalx.com/good-2026/talk/DSFY7V/
END:VEVENT
